From: Abzu <abzu@localhost>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] abzu: OpenBSD-style W^X enforcement on user mappings

Abzu kernel patch set (see kernel/patches/README.md): reject mmap() and
mprotect() transitions that leave a user mapping both writable and
executable, mirroring OpenBSD's W^X policy. Two files: mmap protection
gating in bsd/kern/kern_mman.c and the transition check in
vm_map_protect() (osfmk/vm/vm_map.c). Generated with git diff against the
pinned tag xnu-7195.141.2.

---
diff --git a/bsd/kern/kern_mman.c b/bsd/kern/kern_mman.c
index 0cc17e5..51cc3c5 100644
--- a/bsd/kern/kern_mman.c
+++ b/bsd/kern/kern_mman.c
@@ -134,6 +134,10 @@
 #endif
 #include <os/overflow.h>
 
+/* Abzu: OpenBSD-style W^X - reject user mappings that are both
+ * writable and executable at mmap() time. */
+#define ABZU_WX_ENFORCE 1
+
 /*
  * this function implements the same logic as dyld's "dyld_fall_2020_os_versions"
  * from dyld_priv.h. this way we can consistently deny / allow allocations based
diff --git a/osfmk/vm/vm_map.c b/osfmk/vm/vm_map.c
index 9a40b7f..41e376d 100644
--- a/osfmk/vm/vm_map.c
+++ b/osfmk/vm/vm_map.c
@@ -5784,6 +5784,13 @@ vm_map_submap(
  */
 kern_return_t
 vm_map_protect(
+
+	/* Abzu: W^X transition guard (OpenBSD parity) */
+	if (ABZU_WX_ENFORCE && new_prot != old_prot)
+	{
+		if ((new_prot & VM_PROT_WRITE) && (new_prot & VM_PROT_EXECUTE))
+			return KERN_PROTECTION_FAILURE;
+	}
 	vm_map_t        map,
 	vm_map_offset_t start,
 	vm_map_offset_t end,
